  "goodToKnow": "Die Diagnostik is diagnostics, the field and methods of diagnosis: Labordiagnostik, bildgebende Diagnostik (imaging). One single diagnosis is die Diagnose, and the verb is diagnostizieren. German contributions include Wilhelm Röntgen's discovery of X-rays in Würzburg in 1895, which won the first Nobel Prize in physics; X-rays are still called Röntgenstrahlen in German. It has no plural."
